	m	(I)F	d	m_11761920
		c	@return the height loss of a liquid with the given state compared to a full block.
	m	(Luo;III)I	f_	m_91173234
		c	Returns the depth and falling state of the liquid at the given position, encoded in a 4 bit number,\nor {@code -1} if the given position is not occupied by this liquid.\n<p>\nThe 3 least significant bits encode the depth of this liquid - that is to say, how shallow it lies within this block.\nA value of {@code 0} denotes a source block, while the values {@code 1} to {@code 7} denote increasingly shallow depth values.\n<br>\nIf this liquid is falling, the depth applies not to this liquid, but to the liquid above it.\nIf the liquid above is also falling, the depth is always 0.\n<p>\nThe 4th least significant bit encodes whether the liquid is falling (i.e. there is liquid flowing in from above).
	m	(Luy;III)I	d	m_28266941
		c	@return the depth of the liquid at the given position - that is to say, how shallow it lies within this block -\nor {@code -1} if the given position is not occupied by this liquid.
	m	(Luy;III)Lajr;	i	m_81461875
		c	@return a vector representing the flow direction of this liquid.
	m	(Luy;IIILacn;)D	a	m_22365557
	m	(Luo;III)V	l	m_05783417
		c	Checks for interactions from this liquid with neighboring blocks, e.g. lava turning to obsidian when next to water.
	m	(Luo;III)V	j	m_77303283
		c	Plays sound and particle effects for 'fizzing' lava.
